/-!
# Degree-one generation of the twisted global sections, for an arbitrary graded ring

Let `S = ⨁_{n ≥ 0} 𝒮 n` be a graded ring generated in degree one over `𝒮 0` and let
`X = Proj 𝒮`. This file runs the dévissage of [Stacks, Tag 01YS] clause (5) on `X`: if

* every nonnegative twist of large enough degree has its global sections generated by the
  homogeneous elements of `S` (the hypothesis `hsurj`, with a degree bound `b₀`),
* every coherent module is a quotient of a finite direct sum of twisting sheaves, and
* the first cohomology of the twists of a coherent module vanishes in large degrees,

then for every coherent `ℱ` there is a `B` such that for `d ≥ B` every global section of
`ℱ(1 + d)` is a combination of global sections of `ℱ(d)` with degree-one coefficients.

The three hypotheses are exactly [Stacks, Tag 0AG2], clause (1) and clause (4) of
[Stacks, Tag 01YS] read on `Proj 𝒮`. On projective space the first holds in every degree and the
other two are proved, which is how
`Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.exists_forall_mem_degreeOneSections_of_isCoherent` is proved;
the bound `b₀` is carried because for a graded ring that is not a polynomial ring the degree map
`𝒮 q ⟶ Γ(X, 𝒪(q))` is surjective only in large degrees.

## Main results

All in the namespace `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistDegreeOneStep`.

* `surjective_twistedSectionsAddHom_of_isZero_firstCohomology`: the sections of an epimorphism
  are surjective in the degrees where the first cohomology of the twisted kernel vanishes.
* `mem_degreeOneSections_twistingSheaf`: degree-one generation for a twisting sheaf, in the
  subgroup form.
* `exists_forall_mem_degreeOneSections_of_hasTwistQuotients`: **the dévissage.**

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01YS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01YS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG2)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

